      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Couple of examples of the same thing hapenning with different rigs: the avatar testing rig and my regular avatar. My avatar doesnt have any \"neck\" fixes or anything like that, still get the issue which is amplified if you accidentally calibrate below or above your actual view position. but even when calibrated seemingly perfectly (which is hard to tell sometimes, as you have no in-game indication and you can only remember) the effect is less pronounced, but still noticeable (the spine still turns in a weird way with the head movement).\n\nVery bad calibration (avatar not my proportions) and a quick and dirty calibration on a almost perfectly-proportioned avatar: https://streamable.com/nymtf\n\nBetter calibration on an almost perfectly-proportioned avatar: https://streamable.com/dtf4z\n\nIf we could see like a red orb where our viewing position is btw - that would help calibrating better.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
